{"text": " You wake up in 1720 in Paris. The street smells of horses and everyone's talking about paper. Did you know that this year, France made it illegal to own more than 500 leaves in gold or silver? The government wanted you to trust paper by law. The man behind it is John Law, a Scottish gambler. Like Palmstruck, he was once sentenced to death for killing a man in a duel. Now he runs France's money. One narrow street is packed day and night. People are buying shares in laws, Mississippi company. In about a year and a half, the price has gone up about 40 times. The story goes that a hunchback rents out his back as a writing desk. So what is money now, a belief? It's worth whatever everyone believes it's worth until they don't. By December, the shares have crashed. The notes are losing value and law escapes France. For the next 100 years, people want money they don't just have to believe in. Something they can bite and in London they get it.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 2.12, "text": " You wake up in 1720 in Paris.", "tokens": [50364, 509, 6634, 493, 294, 3282, 2009, 294, 8380, 13, 50502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11481233978271485, "compression_ratio": 1.5068493150684932, "no_speech_prob": 0.010257121175527573, "words": [{"word": " You", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.12, "probability": 0.7606146931648254}, {"word": " wake", "start": 0.12, "end": 0.26, "probability": 0.9884636998176575}, {"word": " up", "start": 0.26, "end": 0.42, "probability": 0.9991858601570129}, {"word": " in", "start": 0.42, "end": 0.52, "probability": 0.99149489402771}, {"word": " 1720", "start": 0.52, "end": 1.42, "probability": 0.9828285872936249}, {"word": " in", "start": 1.42, "end": 1.82, "probability": 0.9314006567001343}, {"word": " Paris.", "start": 1.82, "end": 2.12, "probability": 0.9950329065322876}]}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 2.78, "end": 3.88, "text": " The street smells of horses", "tokens": [50502, 440, 4838, 10036, 295, 13112, 50592], 